fact WorkItem(id: "WI-874", description: some(value: "Declaration-driven guarded-effect evaluation: extract a partial operations guard from its declared CONDITIONAL EFFECT and use it as the runtime guard, instead of hard-coding. A conditional effect E :- G (e.g. Int64.div ... effects { Error[DivisionByZero] :- eq(b, 0) }, int64.anthill:25) is TODAY type-level only (effect inference/refinement, WI-478); its runtime counterpart is hard-coded per-op in Rust (int_div/int_mod/int_rem check == 0 and call raise_division_by_zero — eval/builtins.rs:393/402/415; WI-066/WI-467). PROPOSAL: give a guarded effect OPERATIONAL force. At a partial-op call, read the ops signature effect row (OpSignature.effects, cached, op_info.rs), find the guarded Error effect (EffectExprNode::Guarded { label, guard }, node_occurrence.rs:1159 — guard is a resolvable Value like eq(b,0); label names the effect), substitute params->args, resolve the guard; if it holds -> EVAL raises Error[label] via raise_error_payload (label FROM the declaration, not hard-coded), RESOLVER yields no solution (SLD has no effect machinery). Both the CONDITION and the EFFECT-TO-RAISE come from the declaration; a new partial op (sqrt(x) :- lt(x,0)) inherits the behavior with no evaluator code, retiring the hard-code/declaration divergence risk. FIRST CONSUMER: div/mod/rem/divExact — migrate the eval hard-codes AND the WI-863 case-B resolver div/mod onto this path. EDGES: (1) type-level->runtime is a real semantic addition, commit deliberately; (2) AUDIT every op with a guarded Error effect before enabling; (3) multi-guard ops / guards calling user ops (arithmetic guards are simple eq/neq/lt/gt = easy first case); (4) the SAME partiality is ALSO a constraint (div_nonzero_primary, int64.anthill:39) — use the EFFECT guard as canonical since it names the label; note mod effect-guard eq(b,0) differs from constraint gt(b,0); (5) per-call guard-resolution cost (cheap, guarded ops only). Machinery present: guarded-effect repr (WI-478), raise helpers (raise_error_payload/raise_division_by_zero, eval/effects.rs), op-signature accessor (op_info.rs). SCOPE: Rust — eval/builtins.rs, kb/resolve.rs, a shared guard-extract-and-resolve helper. Soft-follows WI-863 case B. ACCEPTANCE: div/mod/rem by zero raise the declared Error[DivisionByZero] (eval) / yield no solution (resolver) with NO Rust-side == 0 literal in the op builtins; a synthetic partial op with a declared guarded effect and no bespoke Rust guard exhibits the same behavior; full workspace green via rustland/scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
